  "body": "Fixes https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=27820.\n\n@bzbarsky @foolip to review if possible. I went with\n\n>  either the empty string or a string representing the platform on which the browser is executing, e.g. \"Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64\", \"Linux x86_64\".\n\nwhich is similar to but has distinct examples from navigator.platform's \n\n> either the empty string or a string representing the platform on which the browser is executing, e.g. \"MacIntel\", \"Win32\", \"FreeBSD i386\", \"WebTV OS\".\n\nI did this under the assumption that the easiest path for Gecko is to just avoid changing any code. @bzbarsky if you think it'd be better for Gecko to try something like empty string or an alias for navigator.platform, let me know and we can update the spec to say that.\n",
